---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'NQ Answer Retrieval',
  description:
    'Retrieve-then-rerank over 2M Wikipedia passages: 91.0% answer-hit@10 on held-out Natural Questions, without training the retriever on NQ.',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <div class="nq">
    <p class="sans note" style="margin:0 0 8px">Project · Information retrieval · November 2026</p>
    <h1>Finding the answer in 2 million passages, without training the retriever on the test domain</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A retrieve-then-rerank system for open-domain questions from Google's Natural Questions. On 5,712 held-out
      questions it puts a correct answer in the top 10 passages 91% of the time, up from 77%.
    </p>

    <div class="kpis">
      <div class="kpi"><b>91.0%</b><span>answer in top 10 (test; 95% CI 90.2–91.7)</span></div>
      <div class="kpi"><b>95.4%</b><span>answer in top 100 after the first stage</span></div>
      <div class="kpi"><b>+7.0 pts</b><span>gained by removing duplicate passages alone</span></div>
      <div class="kpi"><b>6 min</b><span>of GPU fine-tuning for the 22M-parameter reranker</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="links">
      <a href="/projects/nq-open-rag/paper.pdf">Paper (PDF)</a>
      <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://huggingface.co/NezarIn/nq-open-minilm-reranker"
        >Model on Hugging Face</a
      >
      <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://github.com/Nezarbr/nq-open-demo">Serving code</a>
      <span>Live demo: on request</span>
    </div>

    <h2>The problem</h2>
    <p>
      A question-answering system first has to <em>find</em> the passage that contains the answer. If retrieval misses, nothing
      downstream can recover. The usual Natural Questions benchmarks use retrievers trained on Natural Questions itself. I
      set a stricter rule: the first stage may only use models with no documented Natural Questions training data. That is
      closer to what happens when you point retrieval at a new company's documents.
    </p>
    <p>
      The corpus is the 93,461 Wikipedia page snapshots behind 100,000 NQ questions, cut into 3.2 million chunks.
      Questions are split by row into development (used for every decision) and test (only evaluated, never tuned on).
      The official validation set is a second check.
    </p>

    <h2>How a question is answered</h2>
    <div class="pipe" aria-label="pipeline">
      <div>Question</div><i>→</i>
      <div>Dense search<small>contriever-msmarco, top 500</small></div><i>+</i>
      <div>Keyword search<small>BM25, top 500</small></div><i>→</i>
      <div>Rank fusion<small>RRF, k=60, BM25 weight 0.5</small></div><i>→</i>
      <div>Drop duplicates<small>keep top 50</small></div><i>→</i>
      <div>Rerank<small>fine-tuned MiniLM</small></div><i>→</i>
      <div>Top 10</div>
    </div>

    <h2>Results, stage by stage</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Answer-hit@10: share of test questions (n = 5,712) where a gold short answer appears in at least one of the top 10
      passages. Intervals are 95% Wilson intervals.
    </p>
    <div class="tbl">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th class="barcell"></th><th>hit@10</th><th>95% CI</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr
            ><td>Hybrid retrieval (dense + BM25)</td><td class="barcell"><div class="bar" style="width:77.2%"></div></td
            ><td class="n">77.2</td><td class="n">76.1–78.3</td></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td>+ duplicate removal</td><td class="barcell"><div class="bar" style="width:84.2%"></div></td><td
              class="n">84.2</td
            ><td class="n">83.2–85.1</td></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td>+ ColBERTv2, off the shelf</td><td class="barcell"><div class="bar" style="width:88.4%"></div></td><td
              class="n">88.4</td
            ><td class="n">87.5–89.2</td></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td>+ MiniLM cross-encoder, off the shelf</td><td class="barcell"
              ><div class="bar" style="width:88.4%"></div></td
            ><td class="n">88.4</td><td class="n">87.6–89.2</td></tr
          >
          <tr class="best"
            ><td>+ MiniLM, fine-tuned</td><td class="barcell"><div class="bar" style="width:91%"></div></td><td
              class="n">91.0</td
            ><td class="n">90.2–91.7</td></tr
          >
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">On the official validation split (n = 3,608), the final system scores 91.7 (90.7–92.5).</p>

    <h2>What I learned</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Duplicates were the cheapest win.</strong> 37.8% of the chunks were exact copies, mostly repeated revisions
        of the same article. Removing them freed 43% of the candidate slots and added 7 points without touching a model.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Recall at 100 was already high; ordering was the bottleneck.</strong> The answer was in the top 100 for 95.4%
        of questions but in the top 10 for only 77%, so the effort went into reranking.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Deeper candidate pools did not help.</strong> Reranking 50, 100, 200 or 500 candidates gave the same top-10
        accuracy on development questions, so the system reranks 50.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Two very different off-the-shelf rerankers tied at 88.4.</strong> A few minutes of fine-tuning on training
        questions broke the tie. The biggest gain came at rank 1 (+9.6 points), and table answers improved most.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Approximate search is nearly free on accuracy.</strong> An HNSW index answers in about 1 ms instead of 261
        ms for a 0.7-point loss at hit@100. In the deployed app the reranker dominates latency, so exact search stays.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Deployment</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Docker image built by GitHub Actions</strong> on every push, after a secret scan and an end-to-end test with
        the real models.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Data on a network volume</strong> (1.99M passages, vectors and keyword index), mounted read-only. <strong
          >Compute on demand:</strong
        > a CPU instance that exists only while a demo runs and shuts itself down after three hours.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Deployed equals evaluated.</strong> On 500 test questions, the live code scored 92.2 against 92.4 for the
        evaluated system, with 98.6% per-question agreement.
      </li>
      <li>Latency on 8 CPU cores: 1.7 s median, 2.7 s at the 95th percentile, most of it in the reranker.</li>
      <li>Access is password-protected; the demo is switched on only by me, on request.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The metric is string matching: a passage that mentions the answer by coincidence counts as a hit.</li>
      <li>
        The corpus is the pages behind 100k NQ questions, not all of Wikipedia, so the numbers are not comparable with
        the standard 21M-passage benchmark.
      </li>
      <li>The reranker is fine-tuned on NQ training questions; only the first stage is NQ-free.</li>
    </ul>

    <footer>
      Every number on this page comes from the locked run outputs described in the paper's appendix. Nezar Boujida,
      2026.
    </footer>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .nq {
    --bg: #fbfaf7;
    --fg: #1d1d1f;
    --muted: #5f6368;
    --line: #e3e1dc;
    --card: #ffffff;
    --accent: #2f5d8a;
    --accent-soft: #e6eef6;
    --bar: #9aa9b8;
  }
  .nq {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 16px 80px;
    font:
      17px/1.6 Georgia,
      'Iowan Old Style',
      serif;
  }
  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  .sans {
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin: 48px 0 12px;
    padding-top: 8px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .lede {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
  }
  .kpis {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 24px 0;
  }
  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .kpis {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    }
  }
  .links span {
    font:
      600 14px -apple-system,
      BlinkMacSystemFont,
      'Segoe UI',
      sans-serif;
    color: var(--muted);
    border: 1px dashed var(--line);
    padding: 7px 14px;
    border-radius: 999px;
  }
  .kpi {
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
  }
  .kpi b {
    display: block;
    font:
      600 1.7rem/1.1 -apple-system,
      BlinkMacSystemFont,
      'Segoe UI',
      sans-serif;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .kpi span {
    font:
      13px/1.35 -apple-system,
      BlinkMacSystemFont,
      'Segoe UI',
      sans-serif;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin: 8px 0 0;
  }
  .links a {
    font:
      600 14px -apple-system,
      BlinkMacSystemFont,
      'Segoe UI',
      sans-serif;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    padding: 8px 14px;
    border-radius: 999px;
  }
  .pipe {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font:
      14px/1.3 -apple-system,
      BlinkMacSystemFont,
      'Segoe UI',
      sans-serif;
    margin: 16px 0;
  }
  .pipe div {
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 8px 10px;
  }
  .pipe div small {
    display: block;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .pipe i {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-style: normal;
  }
  .tbl {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    font:
      15px/1.4 -apple-system,
      BlinkMacSystemFont,
      'Segoe UI',
      sans-serif;
  }
  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 9px 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  th {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  td.n {
    text-align: right;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .barcell {
    width: 34%;
  }
  .bar {
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--bar);
  }
  tr.best td {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  tr.best .bar {
    background: var(--accent);
  }
  ol li,
  ul li {
    margin: 6px 0;
  }
  .note {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  footer {
    margin-top: 56px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font:
      13px -apple-system,
      BlinkMacSystemFont,
      'Segoe UI',
      sans-serif;
  }
  .nq h1 {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .nq h2 {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .nq ol {
    list-style: decimal;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }
  .nq ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }
  .nq p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
</style>
